Notebook[{
Cell["The Surface Code at Circuit Level", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d637be9f-f15f-4a82-ad40-2d196fce2dc5"],

Cell["\<\
The distance-3 surface code under CNOT and readout errors, computed with the \
QEC layer\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"717fe7d9-05ce-4b81-b52e-a05f19321d25"],

Cell["\<\
Nine data qubits on a 3\[Times]3 grid carry one logical qubit in the \
distance-3 surface code. Its eight checks, four of X type and four of Z type, \
each act on two or four neighboring qubits. One round of check measurement is \
made by a circuit in which every CNOT fails with probability pC and every \
readout with probability pM. How likely is a decoder to lose the logical \
qubit, and is every single fault still corrected?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b19b6624-1f08-4874-b0a7-71c12a0d4cf4"],

Cell["\<\
Each step below is one call to the QEC layer: the code, its extraction \
circuit, the faults, and the exact logical error rate as a polynomial in pC \
and pM. The last section goes past one round and past distance 3. Every timed \
step prints its wall time in seconds.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"016c1409-4c86-4368-bb22-ba66c39bb6c0"],

Cell["Loading", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"308dfb5c-06e0-4dc1-96db-d6dbda6546f6"],

